build: 2026-06-21 v10.34.29 (AUv3 host — "use plugin instead of Echoel's voice")
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
includes: A loaded plugin can now REPLACE Echoel's built-in voice instead of layering with it. New toggle in Tools ▸ Plugins (on the loaded-plugin bar): "Use plugin instead of Echoel's voice." On, with a plugin loaded, the song drives only the plugin — no doubling, no muddiness; off, the two play together (the previous behaviour). The choice persists across launches and has no effect until you load a plugin. Toggling mid-play is clean: note-offs always fire so the built-in voice never sticks. Completes the basic host loop — discover, load, play your composition, and choose plugin-only or layered. Still to come: hosting effects in a channel insert, the plugin's own interface, saving plugin state, and external MIDI-in into the plugin. Verified: Xcode Compile Check + CI green.
